# Keep the build script
!build.sh

# Per-install runtime state, never source. PluginData holds the player's own
# settings.cfg, their consent record, their session token and (dev builds only) the
# debug bridge's handshake. A `settings.cfg` was committed here once and, because
# build.sh only writes its default when the file is ABSENT, that stale copy meant the
# corrected default was never written — and it was then deployed into every dev
# instance carrying three keys nothing reads (checkInterval, enableKVV,
# enableContractInjection) plus enableCheckpointPhotos=false.
GameData/BoundlessMissions/PluginData/

# ...but keep the bundled third-party assembly, which SHIPS to players and whose
# absence from the repo means a fresh clone cannot build and nothing would ever
# notice the file changing. `*.dll` above would otherwise exclude it.
!GeneKerman/lib/websocket-sharp.dll

# Release artifacts. The GitHub Release is the source of record (see
# PACKAGING.md: the netkan $kref names it), so a copy here is a duplicate that
# never delta-compresses and grows the repo by ~550KB per release forever.
# build.sh --release regenerates it from any tagged commit.
dist/

# Agent guidance for the GK-DW workspace, filter-out for possible private information
/CLAUDE.md
